[node name="MarbleTrapdoor" type="Node3D"]
editor_description = "Target and trapdoor. Origin is the deck at r 53.364 (mid-hole) on a bay centre (+X out, +Z the way the lap runs); the hole is six lane cells, pilaster to pilaster, lip to wall, cut into marble.glb from where these stand: place it (parent at identity), run python3 tools/modelling/maps/marble/marble_build.py --sync-trapdoors (it snaps you to a bay centre), then tools/modelling/model build marble. Shove beside the target, or shoot its plate: 0.3 s rattle, all 24 leaves drop into the spiked pit, open 4 s, close, re-arm 10 s after the pull. Move the target with target_offset / target_yaw_degrees."
